* Super-lead 100 W overdrive head, preamp (see preamp_full.net for the drawing and the reading notes), split in four solvers (amp.json "stages",
* docs/PLAN_CPU.md). preamp_full.net is the whole circuit, the reference the split is checked against (sas_split_check). The stages:
*   preamp.net  V1b (input), the Crunch / Clean and Bright networks, the Normal channel V1a;
*   stage2.net  the Overdrive channel: V2a + V2b;
*   stage3.net  the mixing node, V3b and V3a (cathode follower);
*   stage4.net  V4b, V4a (cathode follower), the tone stack and the Masters.
* A stage's load that sits in the next one is repeated in it (linear parts only; the grids that conduct are not), and the next stage is driven
* through a 1 ohm source at the cut node, so the loaded voltage passes unchanged: node aa (the networks of both channels), V1a's and V2b's plates
* (the mixing node's resistors) and V3a's cathode (the FX divider). The supply is repeated in each stage with the series resistance of the
* rail source scaled by (total current / this stage's current); B+3 and B+4 belong to one stage each, so their networks are unchanged. What is
* lost is the interaction through the shared supply.
*
* This file: stage 1.

.nodes x b4 gin in pkb1 pkb2 pkk1 pkk2 pkk4 ng1 p1 k1 aa bb ov g2a ss r6 r7 nw br bw p1a k1a c7n x1 g3b

V VRAIL x 480.8 378
R R61 x b4 15k
C C37 b4 0 10u
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

R RJ1 in 0 1M
R R2 in ng1 68k
T V1B ng1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R4 b4 p1 220k
R R3 k1 0 1k8
C C1 k1 0 1u

C C2 p1 aa 0.02u
R R5 aa bb 470k
C C3 aa bb 2n
R VR_P1T bb ov 1
R VR_P1B ov 0 1
C C100 bb ov 1n
R R8 ov g2a 470k
R RG2 g2a 0 1G

R SW_CR aa ss 1
R R6 aa r6 470k
R SW_CL r6 ss 1e12
R R7 ss r7 39k
R SW_R7 r7 0 1e12
R VR_P2T ss nw 1
R VR_P2B nw 0 1
C C5 ss br 470p
R R10 br bw 470k
R SW_BRIGHT bw nw 1e12
T V1A nw p1a k1a 12AX7
R R15 b4 p1a 100k
R R16 k1a 0 2k2
C C7 p1a c7n 0.02u
R R17 c7n x1 2M2
C C8 c7n x1 120p
R R18 x1 0 330k
R R21 x1 g3b 220k
R RG3 g3b 0 1G
